# Applies to backend/Dockerfile specifically (BuildKit's <Dockerfile>.dockerignore
# convention: a file next to the Dockerfile it applies to takes precedence over
# the build context root's own .dockerignore). Needed because the repo-root
# .dockerignore deliberately excludes `backend` entirely -- correct for the root
# Dockerfile's frontend build, wrong for this one, which now uses the repo root
# as its context specifically so it CAN see backend/, lib/, and src/types/
# together (see backend/Dockerfile's own header comment for why).
#
# Requires BuildKit (docker/setup-buildx-action + docker/build-push-action
# already use it in CI; modern `docker compose build` defaults to it locally).
# On non-BuildKit Docker this file is silently ignored and the repo-root
# .dockerignore applies instead, which would exclude backend/ and fail the
# build loudly at the first COPY step -- a visible failure, not a silent one.
node_modules
dist
coverage
.git
.venv
**/ml-services/nlu/models
**/ml-services/nlu/.venv
*.sqlite
*.log
npm-debug.log*
android
mcp
docs
archive
e2e
.cursor
